# A data block is a concrete type: an unknown member is a hard error like it is
# on a record or a union. Before, only record/class/union/variant were member-
# strict, so a typo on a data block passed the checker unstamped and surfaced as
# an emitter E0500 with no location.
codes: data { 10 20 30 } out u8

main: function is {
    v: codes.bogus
    print "v=\{v}"
}
